    <string name="keeper_paused">Stock home screen available for 1 minute</string>
    <string name="keeper_title">Replace the TV home screen</string>
    <string name="keeper_body">Fire TV and Android TV don\'t let you choose a Home app. Phone TV can step in front of the stock home screen whenever it appears.\n\nTurn on \"Phone TV home\" under Accessibility. Phone TV only checks which app is on screen; it never reads what\'s on it.\n\nFire TV hides that menu, so use ADB instead:\nadb shell settings put secure enabled_accessibility_services %1$s\nadb shell settings put secure accessibility_enabled 1\n\nExperimental: system updates can block this. Turn it off the same way.</string>
    <string name="keeper_open_settings">Open Accessibility</string>
    <string name="keeper_no_settings">This device has no Accessibility screen. Use the ADB commands shown.</string>
    <string name="keeper_service_label">Phone TV home</string>
    <string name="keeper_service_desc">Brings Phone TV forward when the stock TV home screen appears. Only checks which app is in front; never reads screen content.</string>
    <string name="no_trailer_app">No app found to play trailers</string>
    <string name="update_allow_tv">Allow installs first: Settings › My Fire TV › Developer options › Install unknown apps › Phone TV</string>

